    "rationale": "PNPLA1 transfers linoleate from triglycerides to omega-hydroxyceramides, producing omega-O-acylceramides that are essential components of the stratum-corneum lipid barrier. Loss of PNPLA1 therefore causes a primary acylceramide-synthesis defect. Strongest alternative resolved: The gene is PNPLA1, whose direct biochemical role is linoleate transfer in omega-O-acylceramide synthesis; TGM1 cross-linking is a different ARCI mechanism."
